**IMPORTANT**: Generate ONLY the `pages/index.tsx` file. The _app.tsx and RunList.tsx files will be generated separately.

# GOAL
Build a Next.js dashboard that displays build history and run status in real-time using Convex.

# CONTEXT
This is the visual interface for monitoring Foreman builds. It should be simple, clear, and update in real-time as builds run.

# STACK
- Next.js 14 (App Router or Pages Router)
- React
- Convex React client
- TypeScript

# ARTIFACTS
- `pages/index.tsx`: Main dashboard page ONLY (implementation only, no tests)

NOTE: This file should import RunList from '../components/RunList' - assume that file exists

# FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS

**_app.tsx:**
- Set up ConvexProvider
- Initialize ConvexReactClient with NEXT_PUBLIC_CONVEX_URL
- Wrap entire app

**index.tsx:**
- Show header: "🏗️ PDD Foreman Agent"
- Use useQuery to fetch runs (limit 20)
- Show loading state while fetching
- Show empty state if no runs
- Render RunList component with runs
- Show "Quick Start" section with example commands
- Show sponsor credits in footer

**RunList.tsx:**
- Accept runs array as prop
- Render each run as a card
- Show: spec name, status badge, summary, timestamps, cost, attempts
- Color-code status badges:
  - planning: blue
  - building: orange
  - testing: purple
  - done: green
  - error: red
- Format timestamps as readable dates
- Show duration (endedAt - startedAt)
- Use emoji for status indicators

# NON_FUNCTIONAL_REQUIREMENTS
- Responsive design (mobile-friendly)
- Real-time updates via Convex subscriptions
- Fast load times
- Clean, hackathon-style UI (simple is fine)
- No complex styling (inline styles or simple CSS)

# INTERFACE
```typescript
// pages/_app.tsx
import { ConvexProvider, ConvexReactClient } from 'convex/react';

// pages/index.tsx
import { useQuery } from 'convex/react';
import { api } from '../convex/_generated/api';

// components/RunList.tsx
interface Run {
  _id: Id<'runs'>;
  specName: string;
  startedAt: number;
  endedAt?: number;
  status: 'planning' | 'building' | 'testing' | 'done' | 'error';
  summary: string;
  totalCost?: number;
  attempts?: number;
}
```

# STYLING
Use inline styles or minimal CSS. Example color scheme:
- Background: #ffffff
- Text: #333333
- Borders: #dddddd
- Status colors: as specified above

# VERIFICATION
✅ Dashboard loads without errors
✅ Shows real-time data from Convex
✅ Updates automatically as builds run
✅ Displays all run information clearly
✅ Responsive on mobile
✅ Empty state works correctly

# NOTES
- Keep it simple - this is a hackathon project
- Focus on functionality over fancy design
- Use Next.js 14 patterns (App Router preferred but Pages Router fine)
- NEXT_PUBLIC_CONVEX_URL must be in .env.local
